  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "xvgxiBEyOoLRJGaXBriiDCB+H8w=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:26.661Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "LI.FI's structural argument for why stablecoins replace traditional payment networks in the agentic economy \u2014 card systems cannot:\n\n- **Price micropayments** \u2014 interchange floors sit near 10 cents\n- **Settle continuously** \u2014 clearing runs on business days only\n- **Clear cross-border** without correspondent banks\n\nBy contrast, Circle's gas-free USDC supports transfers as small as **$0.000001** (one millionth of a dollar), settled directly on mainnet, operating 24/7 without banking intermediaries.\n\n**Scale check:** stablecoins already settle ~5x PayPal's volume and nearly half of Visa's.\n\n**Why it matters:** agent workloads are exactly the shape cards exclude \u2014 tiny, constant, borderless.\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:26.661Z"
    }
  },
